# Git — educational use

This folder is a **small teaching example**: one pipeline script, deps, optional bundle export, and generated `artifacts/` after you run `python pipeline.py`.

## What to commit (typical)

| Path | Commit? | Note |
|------|---------|------|
| `pipeline.py` | Yes | All logic |
| `requirements.txt` | Yes | Reproducible installs |
| `README.md` | Yes | How to run |
| `build_project_bundle.py` | Yes | Regenerate `PROJECT_BUNDLE.txt` |
| `../SIMPLE_MLOPS_PIPELINE_PROJECT.md` | Yes | Full spec (repo root) |
| `.gitignore` | Yes | Keeps `.venv` out of Git |
| `artifacts/` | Optional | Educational: commit if you want a “already ran once” demo; skip if you prefer clean clones that always run the pipeline fresh |
